{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF2", "text": "I need to share my production-capacity findings. My check shows that alternate Welding Cell 4 can produce exactly 160 of the 240 assemblies by Friday 16:00, but the remaining exactly 80 assemblies must be produced on Cell 5 after the retrofit. There's also a time constraint: the Cell 4 reservation expires Thursday at noon, and I have not yet entered the temporary reservation in the production system. This means we need to lock in the Cell 4 plan soon, and the Cell 5 retrofit timing directly affects whether we can deliver the full 240 assemblies for the Friday order."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF3", "text": "I need to flag a critical customer quality requirement. I verified in the customer's quality portal that exactly the first 20 assemblies produced after a controller change must be held for weld-macro and dimensional validation before release. This requirement has not yet been copied into our local inspection plan, so it's not reflected in any of our current documentation. This means that after the Cell 5 retrofit, the first 20 assemblies coming off that cell cannot be released to the customer until they pass that validation — this directly impacts how many of the 80 Cell 5 assemblies will be available for the Friday order and needs to be factored into our planning and scheduling."}
```

